    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the Owner API response, following the exact pattern the codebase already uses for the derived `displayName` field.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, right alongside `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the initials as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   For `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec and the acceptance test.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures or errors.",
